  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between etoposide and SBC-1 through a series of target interactions. Etoposide is linked to multiple targets, including Leukocyte common antigen and MFM-223, which in turn are targets of compounds that ultimately direct to SBC-1. These pathways highlight a possible mechanism where etoposide influences downstream targets through a series of molecular interactions, potentially modulating SBC-1 activity. The shared involvement of SBC-1 in multiple pathways underscores its role as a downstream effector, possibly in a broader signaling network. The evidence supports a mechanistic link where etoposide may act through a series of intermediate targets to influence SBC-1, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
